# The decision CHANGELOG is prepend-style (every PR adds an entry at the top), so two overlapping
# PRs routinely conflict there. merge=union keeps BOTH sides on a conflicting merge (no markers)
# instead of failing — concurrent entries auto-combine; re-sort newest-first by hand if the order
# matters. Scoped to the changelog ONLY: decision-registry.md is now the topic-by-topic STATE view
# (the change log moved out to decision-changelog.md in the #143 split, NH-25), and union on a state
# file would silently keep BOTH sides of a real edit — e.g. two PRs flipping the same decision's
# status — with no conflict to review. So the registry is intentionally NOT union and conflicts
# normally. See the changelog "Merge note" + NH-16.
docs/decisions/decision-changelog.md merge=union
